<title>USA: Columbia/HCA Healthcare buys hosptial.</title>
<headline>Columbia/HCA Healthcare buys hosptial.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp said on Friday that it acquired the 135-bed Beckley Hospital in West Virginia for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>In addition, Columbia said its Columbia Raleigh General Hospital, also in Beckley, will immediately begin a review of patient-care services at Beckley Hospital in order to merge operations of the two facilities. Columbia Raleigh General Hospital is a 275-bed acute care hospital.</p>
<p>In particular, the healthcare services provider said it will review the possibility of using Beckley Hospital for outpatient and general support services while it explores expansion plans at Colmbia Raleigh General.</p>
</text>
